From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PowerPhone Build <powerphone@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio: use qualified native q192 speaker path

The final hardware-qualified PowerPhone output uses the guarded native-q192
source-0 profile, two S32 TDM slots at 12.288 MHz, and the one-period-lag D0
transport whose module SHA-256 starts 37cc7ff. Direct tests on physical
amplifiers completed with PCM0,D0 S32_LE/stereo/192000, 1920x2 geometry, a
1920-frame start threshold, zero xruns, and correct native cadence.

Reproduce that transaction in the additive AIDL module while retaining its
7680-frame framework/FMQ scheduling margin. Prepare the legacy PCM exactly
once, feed it one 1920-frame period at a time, and issue
SNDRV_PCM_IOCTL_WRITEI_FRAMES directly. This bypasses pcm_write(), whose error
path clears tinyalsa's private prepared/running state. Hardware observed the
transient EFAULT at byte offset 15360, on the second period after the first was
accepted. Give the first write no retry, permit the bounded 32-by-1-ms retry
only on that second startup write, permanently clear eligibility after it
succeeds, and keep every later failure or xrun terminal.

Both Cirrus Digital PCM Volume controls reset to zero. Snapshot and set only
the selected endpoint to the stock value 817 while both amplifiers and EP1 are
proved off: Digital PCM Volume for earpiece, R Digital PCM Volume for bottom.
Verify that selected control throughout active ownership, and restore it only
after both amplifiers and EP1 are hard-off. Never touch the inactive endpoint's
digital volume.

Pin the final PCM geometry, explicit preparation, exact syscall order,
second-write retry/no-reset behavior, and endpoint-scoped mixer ordering in the
host facade tests.
